parameters.text:
=Incoming message on wire `IntakeAgent_to_ResearchAgent`.

Topic: {{ $json.output.brief.topic }}
Audience: {{ $json.output.brief.audience }}
Focus areas:
{{ ($json.output.brief.key_points || []).map(p => '- ' + p).join('\n') }}

Your web_search step maps to the tools available here: Wikipedia and Tavily_Search (at most 5 searches in total). Compile the research dossier and return it as JSON with keys: dossier.topic, dossier.findings (array of claim, sources, confidence 0-100), dossier.gaps (array), dossier.confidence (0-100 overall), dossier.sources (array of url and title). Never invent sources; mark low confidence where evidence is thin.

={{ $json.round > 0 ? 'Incoming message on wire `ReviewAgent_to_DraftAgent` (revision_round ' + $json.round + ').' : 'Incoming message on wire `IntakeAgent_to_DraftAgent`.' }}

Brief:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.brief, null, 2) }}

Research dossier:
{{ $json.dossier || ($json.research_failed ? '(none: the research step failed, so no verified sources are available)' : '(none: no research was run for this request)') }}{{ $json.round > 0 ? '\n\nPrevious draft (revise this):\n' + $json.previous_draft.content + '\n\nIssues to resolve:\n' + $json.issues.map(i => '- [' + i.severity + '] ' + i.description + ' | suggested fix: ' + i.suggested_fix).join('\n') : '' }}

{{ $json.round > 0 ? 'Revise the draft to resolve every issue.' : 'Write the full deliverable per the brief.' }} Return title, content (the complete deliverable in markdown, meeting the brief's length) and word_count. No placeholder text such as [Insert ...], TODO or TBD. Do not invent facts that are not in the brief or the research dossier: no made-up contact details (emails, phone numbers, extensions), statistics, studies, quotes, names or dates. Cite only sources that appear in the dossier. When a detail is needed but not provided, write around it in general terms.

Note: in this n8n workflow you have no callable tools; perform the steps of your workflow yourself and return only the structured result.

assignments.value:
={{ (() => {
  const len = String($('Build Draft Input').first().json.brief.length || '');
  const nums = /word/i.test(len) ? (len.replace(/,/g, '').match(/\d+/g) || []).map(Number) : [];
  if (nums.length === 0) return true;
  const wc = (($json.output.draft.content || '').trim().split(/\s+/).filter(w => w.length > 0).length);
  return wc >= Math.min.apply(null, nums) * 0.85 && wc <= Math.max.apply(null, nums) * 1.15;
})() }}

={{ (() => {
  const req = String($('Build Draft Input').first().json.raw_request || '');
  const content = String($json.output.draft.content || '');
  const wc = content.trim().split(/\s+/).filter(w => w.length > 0).length;
  const out = [];
  const numWords = { one: 1, two: 2, three: 3, four: 4, five: 5, six: 6, seven: 7, eight: 8, nine: 9, ten: 10 };
  const toNum = s => { const k = String(s).toLowerCase().replace(/,/g, ''); return numWords[k] || parseInt(k, 10) || 0; };
  const ending = req.match(/end(?:s|ing)?\s+(?:with|on)\s+the\s+(?:sentence|phrase|line|words?)\s*:?\s*["“']([^"”']+)["”']/i);
  if (ending) {
    const trim = s => s.trim().replace(/[\s*_"“”']+$/, '');
    if (!trim(content).endsWith(trim(ending[1]))) out.push('The draft must end with the sentence "' + ending[1].trim() + '" and nothing after it.');
  }
  const exact = req.match(/exactly\s+(\d[\d,]*)\s+words?/i);
  if (exact) {
    const n = parseInt(exact[1].replace(/,/g, ''), 10);
    if (Math.abs(wc - n) > Math.max(5, n * 0.05)) out.push('The request asks for exactly ' + n + ' words; the draft has ' + wc + ' (allowed ' + Math.round(n * 0.95) + '-' + Math.round(n * 1.05) + ').');
  }
  const bul = req.match(/(?:bulleted\s+list\s+of\s+at\s+least|at\s+least)\s+(\w+)\s+(?:bullet(?:ed)?\s+)?(?:items?|points?|bullets?)/i);
  if (bul) {
    const n = toNum(bul[1]);
    const have = (content.match(/^\s*[-*•]\s+\S/gm) || []).length;
    if (n > 0 && have < n) out.push('The request asks for at least ' + n + ' bullet items; the draft has ' + have + '.');
  }
  return out;
})() }}

parameters.text:
=Incoming message on wire `DraftAgent_to_ReviewAgent` (revision_round {{ $json.round }}).

Brief:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.brief, null, 2) }}

Draft title: {{ $json.draft.title }}
Draft (markdown):
{{ $json.draft.content }}

Deterministic checks computed by the workflow (treat as facts):
- measured word_count: {{ $json.word_count }} (draft self-reported {{ $json.draft.word_count }})
- length within 15% of the brief's word target: {{ $json.length_ok }}
- placeholder text detected: {{ $json.has_placeholder }}
- explicit request constraints that failed (computed by the workflow, treat as facts): {{ ($json.constraint_failures || []).length ? $json.constraint_failures.join(' | ') : 'none' }}

Original client request (check every explicit requirement in it, not only the brief):
{{ $json.raw_request }}

Evaluate the draft against the brief. Return dimension_scores (clarity, accuracy, completeness, tone_alignment, each 0-100), score (composite 0-100, consistent with the dimensions), requirements (array of requirement + passed boolean), issues (array of severity critical/high/medium/low, description, suggested_fix; empty if nothing to flag) and status (derive it mechanically: "approved" when score >= 80 and no issue is critical or high, else "revision_required"; medium and low issues do not block approval). Flag as high any specific claim (statistic, study, date, contact detail, quote) that is not in the brief or the dossier.

Note: in this n8n workflow you have no callable tools; perform the steps of your workflow yourself and return only the structured result.

parameters.inputSchema:
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "dimension_scores": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "clarity": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "accuracy": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "completeness": {
          "type": "number"
        },
        "tone_alignment": {
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "clarity",
        "accuracy",
        "completeness",
        "tone_alignment"
      ]
    },
    "score": {
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Composite 0-100, consistent with dimension_scores"
    },
    "requirements": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "requirement": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "passed": {
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "requirement",
          "passed"
        ]
      }
    },
    "issues": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "severity": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "critical | high | medium | low"
          },
          "description": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "suggested_fix": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "severity",
          "description",
          "suggested_fix"
        ]
      }
    },
    "status": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "approved | revision_required"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "dimension_scores",
    "score",
    "requirements",
    "issues",
    "status"
  ]
}

assignments.value:
={{ ($json.output.issues || []).concat(
  $('Deterministic Checks').last().json.has_placeholder ? [ { severity: 'critical', description: 'Placeholder text detected in the draft (e.g. [Insert ...], TODO, TBD, lorem ipsum).', suggested_fix: 'Replace every placeholder with real content or remove it.' } ] : [],
  $('Deterministic Checks').last().json.length_ok ? [] : [ { severity: 'high', description: 'Measured word count ' + $('Deterministic Checks').last().json.word_count + ' is outside 15% of the brief length (' + $('Deterministic Checks').last().json.brief.length + ').', suggested_fix: 'Expand or trim the draft to the requested length.' } ],
  ($('Deterministic Checks').last().json.constraint_failures || []).map(f => ({ severity: 'critical', description: f, suggested_fix: 'Revise the draft so that it satisfies this: ' + f }))
) }}

